do_1 = "Defect found at the 7.6 launch on 2026-10-24 (task 7.6, do_2): the bundled hyperfide-qualify server entry (platform/packages/bundled-plugins/dist/hyperfide-qualify/server.js) fails to load with `Cannot find package '@hyperfide/plugin-sdk'`. Cause: platform/plugins/hyperfide-qualify/adapter.ts imports createWorktree and removeWorktree from ../environment-git-worktree/host/worktree.js, a host-only module that drags `@hyperfide/plugin-sdk/host` and packages/environment-provider-host/src/git.ts into the server bundle, and the server runtime (apps/server/src/services/plugins/plugin-runtime.ts, pluginRuntimeExternalUrls) redirects only the bare `@hyperfide/plugin-sdk` specifier. Fix: the qualify server entry imports no host-only module; lane worktree creation and removal go through the environment-git-worktree provider contract on the host side (or a server-safe equivalent), so the prepared server bundle imports only `@hyperfide/plugin-sdk`, Node APIs and bundled dependencies."
do_2 = "A unit test in the plugin suite asserts that the prepared server bundle (prepare.mjs output) contains no `@hyperfide/plugin-sdk/` subpath import, so the regression cannot return silently."
do_3 = "7_7.sh boots platform/apps/server/dist/index.js (building first if dist is missing) with NODE_ENV=production, HYPERFIDE_SKIP_ONBOARDING=true, HYPERFIDE_SERVER_BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1, a free port and a temporary HYPERFIDE_DATA_DIR as the scripts/release.sh smoke does, waits for /health, and asserts with `hyperfide-platform plugin list --json` (HYPERFIDE_SERVER_URL set) that hyperfide-qualify is running without an error, and that the server log under the data dir carries no `plugin hyperfide-qualify failed to load` line."
