do_2 = "The plugin gains an app entry registering a settingsSection rendered on its settings page above the generic fields: connection state from a new RPC railwayStatus (configured yes or no, verified-at timestamp kept in plugin kv, project name, environment name, region, count of sandboxes and of machines created by this provider with lifecycle phase, last redacted error), a `Verify connection` action that resolves the stored settings and calls the Railway API, and the enrollment bootstrap state from src/fleet-bootstrap.ts. The RPC never returns a secret value or fragment and every error passes the existing redaction. Each setting descriptor gets a description telling the owner where to obtain the value. The section follows the settings idiom used by the app (SettingsWithControl, the shared UI kit via tsconfig paths like hyperfide-asks) and reads correctly on mobile."
do_3 = "Tests with the fake client cover railwayStatus unconfigured, configured-and-verified, and a failing verification whose message is redacted. 7_20.sh runs the plugin typecheck and tests and the bundled-plugins build, boots the built server the way 7_7.sh does with no credentials and asserts `hyperfide-platform plugin rpc call hyperfide-machine-railway railwayStatus` answers configured false in under 1 s; it prints each step's seconds and exit code and ends with `ok: 7.20`."
